1
00:00:00,031 --> 00:00:01,448
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,451 --> 00:00:03,031
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,490 --> 00:00:05,615
(Episode 37)

4
00:00:11,781 --> 00:00:14,115
What's this? Lunch just for me?

5
00:00:14,781 --> 00:00:16,823
The staff went out of town
to an arts center.

6
00:00:16,865 --> 00:00:17,948
Thought we'd eat together.

7
00:00:18,251 --> 00:00:19,626
Sure. Sounds good.

8
00:00:28,139 --> 00:00:29,139
Go ahead.

9
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:32,437
You have something to say, so say it.

10
00:00:32,865 --> 00:00:35,948
I'm in a good mood today,
so I'll probably say yes.

11
00:00:37,073 --> 00:00:41,660
Well, I can't go to London this summer.
Let's put it off.

12
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:44,615
- Maybe go in the fall, or...
- Seriously!

13
00:00:44,656 --> 00:00:46,071
Don't be upset.

14
00:00:46,906 --> 00:00:50,281
I just got promoted and settled in.
A long vacation is a bit much.

15
00:00:50,899 --> 00:00:52,274
Please explain it to your dad.

16
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:55,053
Me?

17
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:57,240
I figured you'd know.

18
00:00:57,698 --> 00:01:01,176
How would I know
why Ji Hu isn't going to London?

19
00:01:01,198 --> 00:01:02,403
Then find out for me.

20
00:01:03,406 --> 00:01:05,071
Something about it just doesn't add up.

21
00:01:05,073 --> 00:01:06,862
He said he really doesn't have time.

22
00:01:06,865 --> 00:01:09,698
He has a lot of pieces to see on vacation.

23
00:01:11,158 --> 00:01:12,491
There's so much dust...

24
00:01:17,473 --> 00:01:18,598
Aren't you going?

25
00:01:19,495 --> 00:01:20,662
Yeah. To you?

26
00:01:22,198 --> 00:01:25,406
Of course Do Hee would've
figured something was up.

27
00:01:26,274 --> 00:01:27,729
This is killing me.

28
00:01:27,948 --> 00:01:29,958
I can't exactly confront her about it.

29
00:01:30,906 --> 00:01:32,406
I just wanted to avoid London for now.

30
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:33,905
You're just avoiding it.

31
00:01:33,948 --> 00:01:35,321
Stop dragging this out and come clean.

32
00:01:35,323 --> 00:01:36,989
I know. I'm thinking about it.

33
00:01:37,441 --> 00:01:40,899
It's not just about her and me.
Our families are all tangled up in this.

34
00:01:41,269 --> 00:01:42,946
I don't even know
where to start fixing things.

35
00:01:42,948 --> 00:01:45,783
If you keep dragging this out,
I'm telling Ji Ni.

36
00:01:46,297 --> 00:01:49,406
Hey, what did she ever do to deserve this?
Think how hurt she'd be.

37
00:01:49,865 --> 00:01:50,906
I'm hanging up.

38
00:01:51,781 --> 00:01:53,272
Seriously!

39
00:02:19,567 --> 00:02:22,651
Why are you so quiet?
You haven't eaten anything.

40
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:31,692
- I'm home.
- Welcome home.

41
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,036
Try to get her to eat something.

42
00:02:35,990 --> 00:02:37,031
Okay.

43
00:03:20,781 --> 00:03:22,031
What have you been doing all day?

44
00:03:22,490 --> 00:03:24,740
O Reum must be scared.

45
00:03:25,450 --> 00:03:28,724
Mai, O Reum's okay.

46
00:03:29,031 --> 00:03:30,365
He's gone to a better place.

47
00:03:31,031 --> 00:03:32,454
"A better place?"

48
00:03:33,031 --> 00:03:38,019
Our baby in your belly
hasn't eaten anything all day.

49
00:03:38,734 --> 00:03:39,984
Because you haven't eaten.

50
00:03:40,781 --> 00:03:42,586
I want com nha.

51
00:03:43,073 --> 00:03:45,696
What's com nha? I'll get you some.

52
00:03:45,698 --> 00:03:47,380
My mom's home cooking.

53
00:03:48,031 --> 00:03:49,560
My mom's cooking.

54
00:03:50,490 --> 00:03:51,999
Your mom's cooking?

55
00:03:53,198 --> 00:03:55,602
You don't understand my language.

56
00:03:56,781 --> 00:04:00,987
I'm the only one learning Korean.
I'm the only one living by Korean customs.

57
00:04:02,584 --> 00:04:05,209
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

58
00:04:25,374 --> 00:04:27,511
How long does he have
to keep eating plain porridge?

59
00:04:30,542 --> 00:04:32,125
O Reum.

60
00:04:32,615 --> 00:04:34,573
Just hang in there a little longer.

61
00:04:34,656 --> 00:04:36,323
I don't want to.

62
00:05:13,948 --> 00:05:16,615
O Reum.

63
00:05:21,531 --> 00:05:23,406
O Reum.

64
00:05:25,031 --> 00:05:26,774
Don't interrupt her right now.

65
00:05:27,198 --> 00:05:29,298
Show her to her room. Take it slow.

66
00:05:30,698 --> 00:05:32,698
Do you know why she's acting like this?

67
00:05:34,656 --> 00:05:37,240
I went through something like this
for a while in middle school.

68
00:05:41,198 --> 00:05:43,281
O Reum.

69
00:07:36,323 --> 00:07:39,865
Keep going. That's it.

70
00:07:40,615 --> 00:07:43,531
Good job.

71
00:07:45,031 --> 00:07:46,323
High five!

72
00:07:47,365 --> 00:07:51,406
- One more time.
- One more time.

73
00:07:52,781 --> 00:07:54,990
Good job, O Reum.

74
00:08:03,064 --> 00:08:09,698
Dad.

75
00:09:55,531 --> 00:09:56,720
It's not much.

76
00:09:56,823 --> 00:09:58,365
It's for our living expenses.

77
00:09:58,406 --> 00:10:02,061
Forget it. It's not like I'm a landlord.

78
00:10:02,156 --> 00:10:04,406
How can I just stay here for free?

79
00:10:07,448 --> 00:10:09,452
I have a conscience now.

80
00:10:09,490 --> 00:10:11,990
Anyway, you never let anything slide.

81
00:10:13,490 --> 00:10:17,460
You said you couldn't teach
because of your wrist. Is it better now?

82
00:10:18,031 --> 00:10:19,823
Ji Ni still doesn't know, right?

83
00:10:19,865 --> 00:10:21,363
Of course not.

84
00:10:21,656 --> 00:10:22,978
I got another part-time job.

85
00:10:23,370 --> 00:10:24,766
You don't need to know
what kind of job it is.

86
00:10:24,990 --> 00:10:27,781
I thought this would make
things easier for her.

87
00:10:29,115 --> 00:10:31,917
Even you watch
what you do around your kid.

88
00:10:33,490 --> 00:10:34,656
I'll take it.

89
00:10:35,031 --> 00:10:37,176
That way, you can face Ji Ni
with a clear conscience,

90
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,156
and I need something to tell my kids too.

91
00:10:40,990 --> 00:10:43,156
Your own kids are the hardest to please.

92
00:10:45,365 --> 00:10:46,519
Are you going to singing class?

93
00:10:47,448 --> 00:10:49,448
I have to. I've taken too much time off.

94
00:10:50,656 --> 00:10:52,956
What are you going to do about Sa Bin?

95
00:10:53,198 --> 00:10:54,948
Seung Hyun doesn't seem too keen on him.

96
00:10:55,823 --> 00:10:57,156
You think so too?

97
00:10:58,406 --> 00:11:00,698
Do you need love?

98
00:11:01,406 --> 00:11:02,981
What, you think I don't?

99
00:11:03,490 --> 00:11:05,551
My first love was a disaster.

100
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:08,406
Am I supposed to just be a grandma
until I die? Is that what you want?

101
00:11:08,573 --> 00:11:11,281
Then stop worrying about your kids
and go for it.

102
00:11:11,323 --> 00:11:13,108
You're really stuck in the middle.

103
00:11:13,615 --> 00:11:14,656
Easy for you to say.

104
00:11:15,031 --> 00:11:16,406
I fought for him.

105
00:11:16,615 --> 00:11:19,406
I wouldn't let go.
That's how we ended up living together.

106
00:11:19,531 --> 00:11:21,263
You held on back then.

107
00:11:21,323 --> 00:11:23,573
And now what?
You're just standing there again.

108
00:11:23,615 --> 00:11:25,490
Don't say that just
because it's not your problem.

109
00:11:25,573 --> 00:11:27,448
Is this situation even normal?

110
00:11:27,531 --> 00:11:30,200
That's why I think you're amazing.

111
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:32,948
Even in this situation,
you still want to be in love.

112
00:11:33,406 --> 00:11:36,406
I couldn't do that. My kids come first.

113
00:11:36,490 --> 00:11:39,023
You said Seung Hyun was like
the man of the house.

114
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:43,573
Na Se Ri, are you
trying to gaslight me right now?

115
00:11:44,573 --> 00:11:46,409
Nothing comes without a price.

116
00:11:46,448 --> 00:11:48,424
You don't get anything
by just sitting around.

117
00:11:54,115 --> 00:11:56,117
She keeps going back and forth...

118
00:11:56,490 --> 00:11:57,698
What does she know?

119
00:12:16,031 --> 00:12:17,523
I heard you like this.

120
00:12:18,990 --> 00:12:20,313
Durian.

121
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:24,266
Give me some.
Let me see what it tastes like.

122
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:25,990
Okay.

123
00:12:28,448 --> 00:12:32,347
You just have to get past the smell.

124
00:12:38,281 --> 00:12:39,531
Feeling better?

125
00:12:41,281 --> 00:12:43,837
I have the baby O Reum sent me.

126
00:12:44,031 --> 00:12:49,673
Last night, I dreamed O Reum
was beside me with the baby.

127
00:12:49,990 --> 00:12:52,156
So O Reum finally helped you heal.

128
00:12:55,615 --> 00:12:57,695
I heard I really went off on you.

129
00:12:57,698 --> 00:13:00,823
You did more than that.
You pushed me, and I got hurt.

130
00:13:00,865 --> 00:13:03,971
Really? I'm sorry.

131
00:13:04,156 --> 00:13:07,344
I'm fine. Apologize to your mother-in-law.

132
00:13:07,573 --> 00:13:10,261
Who else does your mother-in-law have?
She only has you three.

133
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,281
Want some?

134
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:16,990
Here.

135
00:13:18,365 --> 00:13:21,286
Milk is good for pregnant women
and women going through menopause.

136
00:13:22,865 --> 00:13:25,281
Second Mother,
are you going through menopause?

137
00:13:25,531 --> 00:13:27,323
It's not like I'm going through puberty.

138
00:13:28,615 --> 00:13:30,696
- Here.
- Thanks.

139
00:13:30,781 --> 00:13:32,031
Try this.

140
00:13:42,781 --> 00:13:44,246
Not really my thing.

141
00:13:46,948 --> 00:13:48,277
It's good.

142
00:13:53,956 --> 00:13:54,998
Mother.

143
00:14:00,365 --> 00:14:03,256
You should eat some too.
It's supposed to be nutritious.

144
00:14:03,281 --> 00:14:04,686
You need it.

145
00:14:04,698 --> 00:14:06,593
Here. Open up.

146
00:14:11,073 --> 00:14:12,673
I'm sorry, Mother.

147
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,372
I'm glad it didn't last long.

148
00:14:16,156 --> 00:14:18,906
Seung Hyun was really worried
about you, you know?

149
00:14:19,031 --> 00:14:21,746
He wanted to take time off
and go to Vietnam with me,

150
00:14:22,115 --> 00:14:24,445
but he said he'd already taken
too much time off.

151
00:14:24,448 --> 00:14:25,656
Let's go in winter.

152
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:27,198
Okay.

153
00:14:41,823 --> 00:14:44,237
I'm sorry to make a model
do something like this.

154
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,483
It's okay.

155
00:14:48,823 --> 00:14:50,961
It's not a big deal.

156
00:14:53,406 --> 00:14:55,906
It's lighter than the first day.
Should I fold the boxes?

157
00:14:55,948 --> 00:14:58,446
No, it's okay. We can use them again
when we clear out inventory.

158
00:14:58,448 --> 00:14:59,490
Okay.

159
00:15:02,115 --> 00:15:04,278
You said this is your first part-time job?

160
00:15:04,281 --> 00:15:06,901
You're really good at this.
And you're strong too.

161
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,865
Selling clothes is harder than it looks.

162
00:15:10,698 --> 00:15:12,073
Don't you think I'm...

163
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:16,496
a little too stylish to work
at a gimbap place?

164
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:20,242
You're right.
Sales have gone up since you started.

165
00:15:20,281 --> 00:15:23,757
I'll pay you a little more,
so don't go work anywhere else.

166
00:15:24,156 --> 00:15:25,948
But who designs the clothes?

167
00:15:25,990 --> 00:15:27,403
My sister does.

168
00:15:27,406 --> 00:15:29,406
She's a fairly well-known designer.

169
00:15:30,490 --> 00:15:33,323
Come to the fashion show next time.
It'll be worth seeing.

170
00:15:33,406 --> 00:15:34,490
You have fashion shows too?

171
00:15:34,531 --> 00:15:37,296
There's a permanent show venue
in Dongdaemun.

172
00:15:42,453 --> 00:15:45,745
You should really model for our show.

173
00:15:46,031 --> 00:15:47,490
Can I recommend you?

174
00:15:48,031 --> 00:15:49,448
I'm not sure about that...

175
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,918
I have other things to do too.

176
00:16:05,281 --> 00:16:06,323
I'm sorry.

177
00:16:20,531 --> 00:16:22,281
Why? What happened?

178
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:25,424
I'm looking for someone.

179
00:16:25,823 --> 00:16:27,758
He looked so much like him.
It startled me.

180
00:16:42,615 --> 00:16:46,701
Honey, I'll be able
to play the cello again, right?

181
00:16:47,990 --> 00:16:53,388
Sometimes I wonder if I ever really
had those years with you and Ji Ni.

182
00:16:55,031 --> 00:16:56,323
Mom.

183
00:16:56,365 --> 00:16:57,988
Hey, Ji Ni.

184
00:16:59,906 --> 00:17:04,153
I wondered how this place was so clean.
So you've been cleaning it.

185
00:17:04,490 --> 00:17:05,573
Who else would?

186
00:17:06,990 --> 00:17:08,434
Were you at a lesson?

187
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:12,906
Where else would I be if not at a lesson?
What brings you here?

188
00:17:13,031 --> 00:17:15,734
I was on my way to a bookstore nearby.

189
00:17:15,906 --> 00:17:19,240
I wanted to have lunch here. Restaurants
are so noisy. Did you eat lunch?

190
00:17:19,249 --> 00:17:21,790
I did. Is some gimbap enough?

191
00:17:21,865 --> 00:17:23,406
Come on. I'll take you somewhere nice.

192
00:17:23,490 --> 00:17:25,240
I'm fine.

193
00:17:26,031 --> 00:17:28,698
I like it here.
It feels like I'm with dad.

194
00:17:28,823 --> 00:17:31,159
You're such a daddy's girl.

195
00:17:35,698 --> 00:17:36,698
Here.

196
00:17:39,990 --> 00:17:42,281
I'm glad this place
hasn't been cleared out.

197
00:17:42,365 --> 00:17:43,944
Right? Me too.

198
00:17:44,490 --> 00:17:45,781
It feels like home.

199
00:17:48,021 --> 00:17:50,855
I'm going to catch Attorney Byeon
no matter what.

200
00:17:51,115 --> 00:17:54,531
I can't let your dad's business
go to waste like this.

201
00:17:55,656 --> 00:17:59,365
By the way, you know Yeong Ju
has fallen in love, right?

202
00:17:59,906 --> 00:18:01,740
Is it still going on?

203
00:18:02,031 --> 00:18:03,573
Apparently.

204
00:18:03,958 --> 00:18:07,208
Even someone like me,
after what happened to O Reum,

205
00:18:07,365 --> 00:18:10,406
I don't think I could do it.
She's pretty amazing.

206
00:18:11,073 --> 00:18:15,611
No wonder she spent her whole life buried
in paperwork and made our lives miserable.

207
00:18:15,698 --> 00:18:19,740
You know that doctor of Korean medicine
well. Help her out.

208
00:18:20,865 --> 00:18:24,198
You can't help love,
and you can't stop it either.

209
00:18:24,323 --> 00:18:25,901
You still haven't learned that?

210
00:18:26,068 --> 00:18:27,610
That's true, but...

211
00:18:28,198 --> 00:18:31,656
she already has to worry
about what people around her will think.

212
00:18:33,281 --> 00:18:36,448
Don't make things worse
by pretending to worry about her.

213
00:18:38,646 --> 00:18:42,642
She's already so easily swayed
by every little thing I say.

214
00:18:42,655 --> 00:18:43,948
It cracks me up.

215
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:46,946
She's spent her whole life alone
because of you.

216
00:18:46,948 --> 00:18:48,988
Wouldn't it be nice
if she could be happy now?

217
00:18:48,990 --> 00:18:50,531
Try to be more kindhearted.

218
00:18:50,823 --> 00:18:52,962
No. I'm jealous.

219
00:18:56,156 --> 00:18:57,448
Seriously.

220
00:18:58,698 --> 00:19:01,176
Is she really dating someone?
That doctor of Korean medicine?

221
00:19:01,406 --> 00:19:02,520
Looks like it.

222
00:19:03,448 --> 00:19:05,168
It's a secret for now.

223
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:06,698
Of course.

224
00:19:08,908 --> 00:19:10,886
So she can still fall in love at her age.

225
00:19:11,115 --> 00:19:13,615
I wonder what I'll do for fun
after I turn 50.

226
00:19:13,656 --> 00:19:16,281
Same. It's hard to imagine.

227
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:21,073
That's amazing.
He's younger, never married, and a doctor?

228
00:19:21,656 --> 00:19:23,365
I hope it works out for her.

229
00:19:23,865 --> 00:19:24,865
Me too.

230
00:19:25,073 --> 00:19:28,281
Your mom took her husband away.
She must've been so lonely.

231
00:19:29,906 --> 00:19:31,448
I'm sorry.

232
00:19:32,156 --> 00:19:34,708
It's okay. I said the same thing.

233
00:19:36,615 --> 00:19:39,636
But, Jung A,
please be a little considerate.

234
00:19:39,865 --> 00:19:42,439
It actually hurts me,
even if I pretend it doesn't.

235
00:19:43,031 --> 00:19:45,198
I'm asking you honestly
because you're my friend.

236
00:19:48,448 --> 00:19:51,369
Could Do Hee really be innocent?

237
00:19:51,781 --> 00:19:52,948
I don't believe it.

238
00:19:53,656 --> 00:19:55,115
There's no evidence.

239
00:19:58,406 --> 00:19:59,490
I'll get going.

240
00:19:59,906 --> 00:20:00,948
Okay.

241
00:20:16,751 --> 00:20:17,918
What are you staring at?

242
00:20:18,990 --> 00:20:20,031
What do you think?

243
00:20:20,656 --> 00:20:21,698
Who?

244
00:20:24,615 --> 00:20:27,059
She seems to be an art teacher.

245
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:29,429
A group of kids came by for her earlier.

246
00:20:29,615 --> 00:20:33,097
Don't her job and vibe fit the show?

247
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:43,158
Do you need anything else?

248
00:20:43,406 --> 00:20:44,406
No.

249
00:20:44,948 --> 00:20:47,302
Excuse me, are you an art teacher?

250
00:20:47,948 --> 00:20:50,115
Yes, I give art lessons
to elementary school students.

251
00:20:50,615 --> 00:20:53,240
- I see.
- Well, then...

252
00:20:58,406 --> 00:20:59,574
She seems good, right?

253
00:21:00,656 --> 00:21:04,640
If you want an art major,
I know someone who might be a better fit.

254
00:21:04,927 --> 00:21:06,990
Really? Is she prettier?

255
00:21:07,073 --> 00:21:08,115
A little.

256
00:21:08,323 --> 00:21:09,365
Is she talkative?

257
00:21:09,823 --> 00:21:13,029
- Does she need to be?
- Hey, we're making a variety show.

258
00:21:13,031 --> 00:21:14,906
We can't cast someone who doesn't talk.

259
00:21:15,990 --> 00:21:18,030
She doesn't talk much,
but she's calm and focused.

260
00:21:18,365 --> 00:21:19,365
That won't work.

261
00:21:19,823 --> 00:21:22,220
I think the owner seems like a good fit.

262
00:21:22,323 --> 00:21:24,375
She was good at chatting
with the kids earlier.

263
00:21:24,531 --> 00:21:25,865
I kept an eye on her for a bit.

264
00:21:28,156 --> 00:21:30,730
Let's go. We'll be late at this rate.

265
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:31,740
Okay.

266
00:21:34,281 --> 00:21:35,365
Have a nice day.

267
00:21:36,073 --> 00:21:37,073
Thank you.

268
00:22:03,490 --> 00:22:05,330
Yes, I saw the artwork you sent.

269
00:22:06,172 --> 00:22:07,910
So far, I like the overall style.

270
00:22:07,990 --> 00:22:12,201
But it needs to be more vibrant
than the previous artwork,

271
00:22:12,865 --> 00:22:14,615
so the difference is clear at a glance.

272
00:22:15,656 --> 00:22:17,775
Please do that. Okay.

273
00:22:19,531 --> 00:22:23,319
With O Reum, you craved spicy rice cakes.
This time, it's cold noodles?

274
00:22:25,156 --> 00:22:28,490
I'm so relieved
to see you smiling like this.

275
00:22:28,906 --> 00:22:30,323
Thank you, Mai.

276
00:22:32,656 --> 00:22:33,740
Hey, you're here.

277
00:22:33,781 --> 00:22:34,781
Yes.

278
00:22:35,740 --> 00:22:37,028
I've already ordered.

279
00:22:37,031 --> 00:22:38,897
Good. I need to get back soon.

280
00:22:39,948 --> 00:22:41,277
Here are your cold noodles.

281
00:22:43,531 --> 00:22:44,880
- Mom.
- Yes.

282
00:22:45,490 --> 00:22:46,606
You're busy, right?

283
00:22:46,698 --> 00:22:49,331
Yes, I haven't done much work lately.

284
00:22:51,781 --> 00:22:55,365
You need to work hard
for our family of four...

285
00:23:01,212 --> 00:23:02,337
Our family of three.

286
00:23:05,698 --> 00:23:09,182
It's okay to cry. Of course it hurts.

287
00:23:09,781 --> 00:23:11,135
You're still a family of four.

288
00:23:11,365 --> 00:23:14,184
Even though O Reum is gone,
you'll always be a family of four.

289
00:23:20,656 --> 00:23:21,698
I'm sorry.

290
00:23:25,073 --> 00:23:27,734
Please eat, honey. I need to eat too.

291
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,561
Are you going to singing class?

292
00:23:36,698 --> 00:23:37,698
Yes.

293
00:23:38,031 --> 00:23:39,948
I've skipped too many classes.

294
00:23:40,031 --> 00:23:42,573
He'll be there too, right?

295
00:23:42,615 --> 00:23:43,656
Who?

296
00:23:47,201 --> 00:23:48,284
He probably will.

297
00:23:56,198 --> 00:23:57,654
- Mrs. No.
- Hello.

298
00:23:57,656 --> 00:23:59,073
- Hello.
- Hello.

299
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:01,154
- The doctor can't come today.
- Really?

300
00:24:01,156 --> 00:24:03,990
I went to him for acupuncture,
and something seemed wrong.

301
00:24:04,198 --> 00:24:06,113
He's usually cheerful,
but he seemed so down.

302
00:24:06,115 --> 00:24:08,531
He's not staying away
because we called him tone-deaf, right?

303
00:24:08,698 --> 00:24:11,115
I already asked him.
He said that wasn't the reason.

304
00:24:11,156 --> 00:24:12,654
Why would you ask him that?

305
00:24:12,656 --> 00:24:14,323
Of course he'd deny it.

306
00:24:15,156 --> 00:24:16,604
I'm sure something else came up.

307
00:24:16,615 --> 00:24:18,156
Shall we warm up our voices?

308
00:24:18,281 --> 00:24:19,323
Yes.

309
00:24:27,198 --> 00:24:30,198
He's usually cheerful,
but he seemed so down.

310
00:24:30,729 --> 00:24:34,979
He seemed so down.

311
00:24:48,156 --> 00:24:49,198
Yes.

312
00:24:55,073 --> 00:24:56,584
Aren't you going to singing class?

313
00:24:56,740 --> 00:24:57,781
No.

314
00:24:58,448 --> 00:24:59,573
Thank you.

315
00:25:06,031 --> 00:25:07,446
You asked me to make it hot, so...

316
00:25:08,073 --> 00:25:09,696
- I'm so sorry.
- It's fine.

317
00:25:09,698 --> 00:25:11,823
I wasn't careful.

318
00:25:11,990 --> 00:25:13,031
Well, then...

319
00:25:23,156 --> 00:25:26,448
When someone chooses love,
no one can stop them.

320
00:25:26,490 --> 00:25:27,781
Just like you.

321
00:25:28,156 --> 00:25:32,073
If Yeong Ju wants things to stay familial,

322
00:25:32,448 --> 00:25:33,906
that may be how she truly feels.

323
00:25:34,073 --> 00:25:35,823
You should respect that too.

324
00:25:45,323 --> 00:25:48,781
If her sons are against it,
she probably won't budge.

325
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:35,317
Doctor, a patient is waiting for you.

326
00:26:35,865 --> 00:26:36,948
Okay.

327
00:26:43,573 --> 00:26:44,820
Did you eat lunch?

328
00:26:44,823 --> 00:26:47,172
Yes, Ji Ni. Did you?

329
00:26:47,531 --> 00:26:48,784
I did.

330
00:26:50,865 --> 00:26:53,952
Tae O, I have a big problem.

331
00:26:54,073 --> 00:26:56,955
All the notes I'd been making
were saved on my tablet,

332
00:26:58,588 --> 00:27:00,588
and I can't remember any of them.
What should I do?

333
00:27:10,656 --> 00:27:11,698
Ji Ni.

334
00:27:13,615 --> 00:27:14,656
Here.

335
00:27:21,156 --> 00:27:22,881
You were right. Do Hee took it.

336
00:27:23,740 --> 00:27:26,156
I'm sorry I didn't believe you.

337
00:27:30,573 --> 00:27:32,670
I found it at Do Hee's place. But...

338
00:27:33,156 --> 00:27:35,299
she still doesn't know I found it.

339
00:27:40,406 --> 00:27:42,487
What do you want to do?
Should we confront her?

340
00:27:42,490 --> 00:27:44,592
I'll be your witness. I found it myself.

341
00:27:48,638 --> 00:27:49,820
I'll wait.

342
00:27:49,823 --> 00:27:51,057
Wait for what?

343
00:27:52,198 --> 00:27:54,641
She must've stolen it for a reason.

344
00:27:55,073 --> 00:27:56,498
We'll find out soon...

345
00:27:57,531 --> 00:27:59,889
why she did this.

346
00:28:27,028 --> 00:28:30,320
(Family Register)

347
00:28:30,323 --> 00:28:32,113
Why? Are you afraid
your sons might see us?

348
00:28:32,115 --> 00:28:33,446
For now, yes.

349
00:28:33,448 --> 00:28:37,404
If you're not on my side,
who can I talk to?

350
00:28:37,406 --> 00:28:39,363
Then let's have some fun.

351
00:28:39,365 --> 00:28:40,613
Will Ji Ni really be fired?

352
00:28:40,615 --> 00:28:41,904
We'll have to part ways.

353
00:28:41,906 --> 00:28:44,031
You've caused a huge problem,
and now I'm in trouble too.

354
00:28:44,073 --> 00:28:45,365
Do you think I'll let this slide?

355
00:28:45,490 --> 00:28:48,615
I told you. I'm not who I used to be.

356
00:28:50,626 --> 00:28:52,626
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
